Camera codec probe limits and diagnostics
=========================================

Codec discovery discards FFprobe stderr because native diagnostics can contain
RTSP credentials. Application warnings contain fixed categories and the child
exit code, not the RTSP URL, vendor reply, native output or transport exception.
Previously stored logs are not rewritten by this change.

The probe accepts at most 1 MiB of stdout and uses a 15-second execution timeout.
Timeout or oversized output returns unknown metadata. Cancellation propagates
after killing the owned child and draining its pipe. Child creation failures
return a fixed StreamError. Normal H.264/HEVC codec metadata remains available;
malformed JSON shapes, unsafe codec names and invalid dimensions/bitrates do not
become arbitrary response text. Missing or invalid fields remain unknown/zero.

Regression tests use real harmless OS children with synthetic output, including
native secret markers, cancellation, timeout, oversize JSON and malformed
metadata. They do not contact cameras or claim vendor/RTSP interoperability.
The packaged FFprobe binary and full candidate need separate runtime qualification.

This is codec-probe lifecycle work only. It does not change FFmpeg HLS ownership,
coordinate API workers or hosts, bound the private HLS stderr file, provide
per-viewer leases, or fence camera permission changes after their final check.
